      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Directly lying is the biggest risk here, as subsequent evidence will undermine any statement you make now. Instead of \"no,\" pivot to a commitment to transparency regarding *investigation status*, not attack status. You could state, \"At this moment, we have no evidence of a confirmed unauthorized access event that warrants public disclosure, but we are actively and thoroughly investigating all potential system anomalies to ensure complete security for our users.\" This is truthful to the *current state of evidence* while controlling the narrative.",
